// This test was briefly gated off Windows for runtime crashes observed
// mid-bringup: the dev half was the `-g` opaque-FFI data-layout defect
// (fixed before the gate was revisited), and the release stack overflow
// has not reproduced since — on x86_64-pc-windows-msvc both profiles now
// build and run correctly, with the linked binary carrying exactly one
// folded `REUSSIR_TAG_DUMMY` definition (the cross-unit immediate
// identity the overflow signature had implicated).

// A statistics pipeline as a two-package `rene build`: stdin is parsed
// into the runtime's rc vector inside `vecio`'s textures (bad tokens
// skipped Rust-side), and everything after the boundary is functional
// Reussir — a closure-compared merge sort over a cons-list, the summary,
// and a histogram bucketed by threshold comparison. The release profile is
// the interesting build: three codegen units plus reuse-across-call, with
// the polyffi bitcode linked into the split module set.

// RUN: %rene build --manifest-path %S/stats/rene.ncl --build-dir %t.bdir %rrc_linker | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LISTING

// LISTING: {{[/\\]}}dev{{[/\\]}}stats

// RUN: %t.bdir/dev/stats%exe_ext < %S/stats/example.in | %FileCheck %s

// Eight parseable samples (the `oops` token is dropped by the reader):
// sorted range 4 to 120.25, an exact mean, the even-count median averaged
// from the two middle samples, and a range histogram with the low bucket
// holding five of the eight.
// CHECK:      n 8
// CHECK-NEXT: min 4.00
// CHECK-NEXT: max 120.25
// CHECK-NEXT: mean 40.00
// CHECK-NEXT: median 19.75
// CHECK-NEXT: bucket 0: #####
// CHECK-NEXT: bucket 1: #
// CHECK-NEXT: bucket 2: #
// CHECK-NEXT: bucket 3: #

// No input is a report, not a crash.
// RUN: echo | %t.bdir/dev/stats%exe_ext | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EMPTY

// EMPTY: no samples

// The split, optimized build (three codegen units, reuse-across-call) is
// the same pipeline.
// RUN: %rene build --manifest-path %S/stats/rene.ncl --build-dir %t.bdir --profile release %rrc_linker | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RELEASE
// RUN: %t.bdir/release/stats%exe_ext < %S/stats/example.in | %FileCheck %s

// RELEASE: {{[/\\]}}release{{[/\\]}}stats
